From: Rico Rojas <rickrojas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:31:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(meeting): allow self-hosted transcription for Note
 Recording

Self-hosted mode was hard-blocked for meetings: the routing helper threw
"not supported for Note Recording" and the settings card was disabled
with a coming-soon badge. Self-hosted is a batch HTTP endpoint, not a
realtime socket, so it now reuses the chunked local meeting pipeline
(buffer PCM, downsample, WAV) and POSTs each chunk to
<url>/audio/transcriptions with the configured model and language.

- meetingTranscriptionRouting resolves {provider:"self-hosted",
  endpoint, model, language}; throws only when the URL is empty
- meetingRecordingStore passes the meeting-scoped URL and global model
- MeetingSettings enables the mode and renders SelfHostedPanel
- main process accepts self-hosted in prepare/start, transcribes chunks
  through the new pure selfHostedMeetingTranscription helper
- closure tests skip self-hosted like local (no socket, no token)

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015uYKeUK2xoKRQMj5gCikCq
